WEBVTT

00:15.015 --> 00:17.225
[theme music playing]

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:01.061 --> 01:04.439
SEOUL OLYMPIC SWIMMING POOL

01:07.609 --> 01:11.071
[coach] Seung-hyo, is your mom here?
Wasn't she coming to Korea for the match?

01:11.154 --> 01:13.490
No, something urgent came up,
so she couldn't make it.

01:13.573 --> 01:15.867
[coach] Is that so? What about your dad?

01:15.992 --> 01:19.746
A lot of his patients need critical care,
so he couldn't leave the hospital.

01:19.829 --> 01:22.165
They're important.
You get it, right?

01:22.248 --> 01:23.541
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

01:23.625 --> 01:24.959
Let's focus on the meet.

01:25.043 --> 01:27.420
You'll make the national team if you win.

01:29.172 --> 01:32.717
[female announcer] The 200-meter
freestyle finals will begin shortly.

01:32.801 --> 01:33.635
Let's go!

01:37.222 --> 01:39.140
[audience cheering]

01:41.184 --> 01:42.435
[exhales]

01:47.232 --> 01:48.733
HYEREUNG HIGH SCHOOL SWIM TEAM

01:51.778 --> 01:52.695
[exhales]

01:53.196 --> 01:56.825
[announcer] In lane 8, Choi Seung-hyo
from Hyereung High School.

01:56.908 --> 01:58.409
[Seok-ryu] You can do it, Seung-hyo!

01:58.993 --> 02:01.329
Choi Seung-hyo from Hyereung High
in lane 8! Let's go!

02:01.412 --> 02:03.248
What on earth? Why is she here?

02:03.331 --> 02:05.250
Hey, Seung-hyo! Over here!

02:05.333 --> 02:07.752
- Over here!
- Please, stop calling my name.

02:07.836 --> 02:11.214
Let's go, Seung-hyo! Crush them!
Leave them in the dust!

02:11.297 --> 02:12.966
Jeez, Seok-ryu.

02:13.049 --> 02:15.885
If you don't win,
don't even think of coming back home!

02:15.969 --> 02:16.886
[Seung-hyo groans]

02:16.970 --> 02:18.847
- [whistle blows]
- [audience cheering]

02:18.930 --> 02:19.848
You can do it!

02:20.515 --> 02:22.142
[upbeat music playing]

02:27.856 --> 02:30.525
- [whistle blows]
- [male announcer] Take your marks.

02:34.612 --> 02:35.530
[exhales]

02:37.866 --> 02:38.783
[buzzer sounds]

02:39.617 --> 02:42.495
- [audience cheering]
- Let's go!

02:45.165 --> 02:46.082
Go!

02:46.166 --> 02:48.168
You're doing great!

02:48.751 --> 02:49.752
Come on!

02:51.171 --> 02:52.338
Let's go!

02:56.968 --> 02:57.969
CHOI SEUNG-HYO
SIXTH

02:58.052 --> 03:00.054
It's okay! Keep going!

03:04.142 --> 03:07.604
Go, go, go!

03:11.232 --> 03:12.317
Hey!

03:12.400 --> 03:13.985
- [Seok-ryu exclaims]
- [Seung-hyo groans]

03:14.068 --> 03:15.403
[dogs barking in distance]

03:17.864 --> 03:19.365
Wow.

03:19.449 --> 03:21.784
She seriously must be crazy.

03:22.577 --> 03:25.371
Wow, seriously?

03:26.247 --> 03:27.957
Do you know what time it is?

03:28.041 --> 03:31.711
I don't.
Look at your watch if you're so curious.

03:31.794 --> 03:33.254
You think I'm asking for the time?

03:33.338 --> 03:36.466
- Don't you get what's implied?
- Gosh, he's loud.

03:37.216 --> 03:41.262
College entrance exams were ages ago.
What's with the comprehension questions?

03:41.346 --> 03:42.805
It's 3:00 a.m.

03:42.889 --> 03:45.141
Even the birds and lambs are asleep.

03:45.225 --> 03:47.518
So why am I hearing your screams?

03:47.602 --> 03:50.146
Goodness, poor Seung-hyo.

03:50.230 --> 03:51.856
Did I wake our precious baby?

03:51.940 --> 03:53.024
Don't do that.

03:54.067 --> 03:57.028
Our baby can't sleep?
Do you want me to sing you a lullaby?

03:57.111 --> 03:58.696
Hey, stop talking like that.

03:58.780 --> 04:01.783
Then, go back inside and sleep
if you don't want to hear it.

04:01.866 --> 04:02.867
You're so loud.

04:08.915 --> 04:10.083
Hey, in that movie,

04:10.208 --> 04:11.876
the curly-haired one is the ghost.

04:14.003 --> 04:16.798
Hey, did you just say a spoiler?

04:17.257 --> 04:19.884
That's so unethical!
How could you reveal a spoiler?

04:20.009 --> 04:22.178
This isn't The Sixth Sense!
Curly-haired?

04:22.262 --> 04:25.014
I'll make sure you don't sleep tonight!

04:25.098 --> 04:26.975
You have serious character issues.

04:29.560 --> 04:30.770
[upbeat music playing]

04:31.854 --> 04:33.189
[audience exclaiming]

04:34.023 --> 04:36.693
Hey! Keep going! Just a little more!

04:36.776 --> 04:40.863
You're doing great! Let's go!
Go all the way!

04:46.703 --> 04:47.829
[music fades]

04:59.382 --> 05:00.550
FIRST PLACE
CHOI SEUNG-HYO

05:00.633 --> 05:02.051
[audience cheering]

05:04.470 --> 05:05.847
[exclaiming]

05:05.930 --> 05:07.890
- Hey, you came in first!
- [chuckles]

05:08.558 --> 05:10.977
- You did great!
- [chuckles]

05:11.060 --> 05:12.729
[upbeat music playing]

05:12.812 --> 05:14.355
Great job!

05:15.690 --> 05:16.899
[Seung-hyo exhales]

05:17.734 --> 05:21.904
STOP LINE

05:21.988 --> 05:23.156
[whistle blows]

05:40.673 --> 05:41.758
[panting]

05:58.483 --> 06:00.193
She's quiet now that it's morning.

06:13.414 --> 06:15.666
Seung-hyo, you're up early.

06:16.125 --> 06:17.794
- Yes.
- I didn't see you come in.

06:17.877 --> 06:18.795
Did you work late?

06:19.378 --> 06:21.047
- Yes.
- How worrisome.

06:21.130 --> 06:22.131
My son's working so hard.

06:22.590 --> 06:23.716
It's fine.

06:24.258 --> 06:26.594
Come down after you wash.
Let's have breakfast.

06:27.178 --> 06:28.096
[door opens]

06:28.805 --> 06:29.639
[door closes]

06:44.612 --> 06:45.655
[cutlery clinking]

06:55.414 --> 06:58.084
I wanted to make some jambon-beurre.

06:59.168 --> 07:01.170
But I didn't have the right ingredients.

07:01.754 --> 07:03.673
We used to eat it at times in France.

07:03.756 --> 07:04.590
Do you remember?

07:05.216 --> 07:06.050
No, I don't.

07:07.009 --> 07:09.345
Right? You were so young.

07:11.264 --> 07:13.307
Still, since we're together…

07:15.393 --> 07:17.019
It's nice to eat together.

07:17.103 --> 07:20.648
I never imagined you'd come back
to live here with us.

07:20.731 --> 07:23.025
It's close to work. That's all it is.

07:24.652 --> 07:26.654
Did you clear out your studio apartment?

07:27.405 --> 07:30.283
Yes, building an office building
wasn't easy.

07:30.366 --> 07:32.493
If it's about money,
you should've told me.

07:33.703 --> 07:36.122
Architecture is a business too.
Don't overdo it.

07:36.747 --> 07:37.874
Yes, sir.

07:37.957 --> 07:39.625
Always be careful on site too.

07:40.126 --> 07:42.753
We get a lot of injured workers in the ER.

07:42.837 --> 07:43.671
I will.

07:48.259 --> 07:49.385
Thanks for breakfast.

07:53.806 --> 07:57.059
This toast tastes awful.

07:59.103 --> 08:02.273
I'll buy some baguettes
and butter for tomorrow.

08:02.398 --> 08:04.775
There's no need.
I usually don't eat breakfast.

08:06.194 --> 08:07.028
Really?

08:12.909 --> 08:14.327
When are you being assigned?

08:14.410 --> 08:15.411
[chuckles softly]

08:16.412 --> 08:19.332
You asked the same question as your dad.

08:19.415 --> 08:21.459
Why? Do you want me to leave again?

08:22.168 --> 08:23.002
It's not that…

08:26.422 --> 08:29.300
You don't like staying in Korea
for long periods.

08:38.309 --> 08:40.436
Thank you for breakfast.
I'm off to work.

08:49.695 --> 08:51.322
[door sliding]

08:51.948 --> 08:53.366
- [exhales]
- [door sliding]

08:57.036 --> 08:58.329
[loud pop]

08:59.413 --> 09:00.665
[Na-yun] Congratulations!

09:00.748 --> 09:01.916
Gosh, you scared me.

09:03.334 --> 09:07.421
Did you deliberately set off
an explosion at me?

09:07.505 --> 09:10.716
What? No, it's a party popper
from Hyeong-chan's birthday party.

09:10.800 --> 09:12.468
No, that's an explosive device.

09:12.552 --> 09:15.012
Don't you know people have died
from those things?

09:15.096 --> 09:17.473
An architect
who disregards safety is trouble.

09:17.557 --> 09:19.183
I'm the one who's troubled.

09:19.267 --> 09:21.477
I'm getting an earful
for congratulating you.

09:21.936 --> 09:23.604
Congratulate me for what?

09:23.688 --> 09:27.233
Hey, Seung-hyo! We did it!

09:27.316 --> 09:28.651
Mr. Yoon will tell you.

09:29.735 --> 09:31.279
What is it? What's going on?

09:31.404 --> 09:33.489
[Myeong-u] We can finally breathe.

09:33.573 --> 09:35.741
We got a huge offer.

09:35.825 --> 09:39.453
A term reserved
for only the top 1% of Korea.

09:40.079 --> 09:42.123
A prestigious retirement community.

09:43.499 --> 09:46.877
Danyeong Medical Foundation
is partnering with YR Group to build it,

09:46.961 --> 09:48.879
and they came
directly to us to oversee it.

09:48.963 --> 09:49.839
[exhales]

09:49.922 --> 09:52.425
She said something would happen
in the latter half of the year.

09:52.508 --> 09:54.844
- Hye-ran was right.
- Your wife went to a fortune teller?

09:55.469 --> 09:57.221
Yeah. It was tarot cards this time.

09:58.556 --> 10:02.059
We're riding
on the colossal wheels of fortune.

10:02.143 --> 10:03.311
POMEGRANATE TREE

10:03.394 --> 10:04.895
The leaves look a bit dry.

10:04.979 --> 10:08.858
You're worried
about that measly plant right now?

10:08.941 --> 10:11.068
- Someone cast a curse.
- [Myeong-u] What?

10:11.152 --> 10:13.029
[Seung-hyo] Our company's
fate rests on it.

10:13.154 --> 10:14.739
We'll shut down if it withers.

10:14.822 --> 10:16.907
Goodness. Why didn't you water it?

10:16.991 --> 10:18.534
No, never mind.

10:18.618 --> 10:20.911
Can someone go
and buy some plant nutrients?

10:20.995 --> 10:22.705
You're such a slave to superstitions.

10:22.788 --> 10:25.583
That's how desperate I am.

10:25.666 --> 10:27.168
If this deal goes through,

10:27.251 --> 10:31.172
we won't have to worry about anything
for a while! We have to risk it all!

10:31.255 --> 10:32.089
I want to do this.

10:32.173 --> 10:35.343
Of course. But we can't just do it.
We have to do it well.

10:35.426 --> 10:36.302
I want to do it.

10:36.385 --> 10:38.971
I want to do it too.
I want to do it so badly!

10:39.055 --> 10:41.057
No, I want to see you do it!

10:44.810 --> 10:47.855
HYEREUNG HIGH GYM REMODELING
AND EXPANSION DESIGN COMPETITION

10:49.106 --> 10:50.066
Mom.

10:52.360 --> 10:53.194
Mom?

10:54.862 --> 10:55.696
Is no one home?

11:03.496 --> 11:05.373
[Mi-suk] I made curry.
Heat it up and eat it.

11:06.290 --> 11:08.709
Why is she suddenly being so sweet?

11:11.545 --> 11:12.963
[playful music playing]

11:24.975 --> 11:26.143
[Mi-suk humming]

11:28.979 --> 11:30.815
A hundred rolls of kimbap.

11:30.898 --> 11:33.526
Where did this incredible order come from?

11:34.110 --> 11:36.987
I don't know.
They're snacks for some TV shoot.

11:37.071 --> 11:38.406
They'll pick them up at 6:00 p.m.

11:38.489 --> 11:41.325
Is that so?
I'll ask what they're shooting later.

11:41.909 --> 11:45.371
So you've decided to leave Seok-ryu be?

11:46.831 --> 11:48.124
- Yeah.
- Really?

11:49.208 --> 11:50.167
What for?

11:50.251 --> 11:53.045
It's called the Romeo and Juliet effect.

11:53.129 --> 11:56.799
They say love becomes more intense
the more the parents interfere.

11:56.882 --> 11:58.843
[laughingly] What does that
have to do with this?

11:58.926 --> 11:59.802
Keep listening.

11:59.885 --> 12:03.597
It's an absolute truth that applies
to other areas as well, not just love.

12:03.681 --> 12:05.933
The more parents oppose
and try to control their child,

12:06.016 --> 12:07.726
the more the child rebels.

12:07.810 --> 12:09.937
Yeah, you're right.
You made a good choice.

12:10.020 --> 12:13.107
You should be as gentle
when rolling kimbap too.

12:13.190 --> 12:15.818
If you try to keep things in by force,
the sides…

12:15.901 --> 12:17.653
[Mi-suk humming]

12:19.447 --> 12:22.450
Seok-ryu won't last long.

12:22.533 --> 12:23.951
How do you know that?

12:24.034 --> 12:26.120
Not just anyone can be unemployed.

12:26.203 --> 12:28.330
She's been diligent her whole life.

12:30.833 --> 12:33.627
She'll end up caving in on her own
with a slight nudge.

12:34.545 --> 12:36.046
I'm waiting for that moment.

12:38.215 --> 12:39.049
It'll come soon.

12:39.717 --> 12:41.927
We need to make 100. How can you eat that?

12:42.011 --> 12:44.847
It's so good. I'm just tasting it.

12:44.930 --> 12:46.098
- Is it good?
- Yeah.

12:46.182 --> 12:47.016
Hurry up!

12:49.351 --> 12:50.644
[quirky music playing]

12:50.728 --> 12:51.687
[keys clacking]

13:06.327 --> 13:07.203
[inhales]

13:08.412 --> 13:09.747
Done.

13:11.248 --> 13:15.044
BAE SEOK-RYU'S UNEMPLOYED SCHEDULE

13:15.127 --> 13:17.963
PLAY GAMES

13:18.047 --> 13:18.923
[clock ticking]

13:19.006 --> 13:19.840
Nice.

13:24.053 --> 13:29.934
SPACE OUT

13:31.477 --> 13:32.853
[indistinct sounds over TV]

13:33.479 --> 13:35.272
I'd be so good at that.

13:35.356 --> 13:36.774
WATCH TV

13:36.857 --> 13:39.735
They're not doing it right.
You can't do it like that.

13:44.365 --> 13:45.282
[chuckles softly]

13:47.826 --> 13:49.828
TAKE A NAP

14:01.674 --> 14:02.633
[music fades]

14:08.430 --> 14:09.348
[line ringing]

14:09.890 --> 14:10.891
[phone vibrating]

14:14.645 --> 14:16.230
- What's up?
- I'm busy. Bye.

14:16.313 --> 14:20.609
Wait. I didn't even tell you why I called.
What if it's important?

14:20.693 --> 14:22.319
What is it?

14:22.403 --> 14:25.114
The one with straight hair was the ghost.

14:25.197 --> 14:26.031
I'm hanging up.

14:26.115 --> 14:27.992
[Seok-ryu] Wait! It's important.

14:28.659 --> 14:31.287
- Let's go read comic books.
- You may not know this.

14:31.370 --> 14:33.372
But people with jobs work on weekdays.

14:33.455 --> 14:35.124
Hey, I didn't mean now.

14:35.207 --> 14:38.794
I plan to be there
from 6:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m.

14:38.878 --> 14:40.462
Come when you get off work.

14:40.546 --> 14:42.172
No. I'm hanging up now.

14:43.507 --> 14:44.466
[call disconnects]

14:46.260 --> 14:47.094
Heartless jerk.

14:48.429 --> 14:51.599
Forget it. I have other friends. [scoffs]

14:54.268 --> 14:56.020
- [man] Welcome.
- [Mo-eum] Hello.

14:57.438 --> 14:58.272
[Seok-ryu] Hey!

14:58.355 --> 14:59.815
[song playing in background]

14:59.899 --> 15:01.066
My best friend.

15:01.150 --> 15:03.110
My very close and long-time friend!

15:03.193 --> 15:05.237
What's with all the flattery?

15:05.321 --> 15:07.823
I didn't even get most of it.

15:08.407 --> 15:11.827
Mo-eum, you're so gloomy.
Did you have a hard day?

15:11.911 --> 15:15.205
Seok-ryu, you're so cheerful.
Did you have fun doing nothing?

15:15.289 --> 15:16.123
Of course.

15:16.832 --> 15:18.083
What do you want to read?

15:18.167 --> 15:19.835
I got something from every genre.

15:19.919 --> 15:21.378
Romance? Martial arts? Shonen manga?

15:21.462 --> 15:23.964
[sighs] They all sound boring.

15:25.174 --> 15:26.175
Oh!

15:26.258 --> 15:27.301
FOR ADULTS ONLY

15:27.384 --> 15:28.510
I want something red.

15:28.594 --> 15:29.970
I see.

15:32.097 --> 15:34.642
We're in a public space
in my neighborhood.

15:36.435 --> 15:38.062
I've never seen anyone so brave.

15:38.604 --> 15:39.647
Right?

15:39.730 --> 15:42.733
I took a peek earlier.

15:42.816 --> 15:45.277
See Rose of Bliss?
It looked pretty good.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.571
Grab it when no one's watching.

15:47.655 --> 15:49.323
Pass it to me when you're done.
Okay? Go.

15:49.406 --> 15:50.574
Now. No one's watching.

15:50.658 --> 15:51.992
- Right now.
- Seok-ryu?

15:52.743 --> 15:55.162
That's not the "red" I was talking about.

15:56.038 --> 15:59.416
Something with fresh blood and torn flesh!
Things like that.

15:59.917 --> 16:01.168
Like those.

16:01.251 --> 16:04.213
That type of red? You could've told me.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.176
Hello.

16:10.469 --> 16:12.054
Your other best friend's here.

16:13.889 --> 16:15.724
- [quirky music playing]
- [sighs]

16:15.808 --> 16:19.186
Nope. As of today, he's out.
He's been disqualified.

16:22.481 --> 16:23.649
You won't even say hi?

16:23.732 --> 16:25.985
You came. You said you wouldn't.

16:26.068 --> 16:29.029
I didn't come for you.
There's a book I wanted to read.

16:29.113 --> 16:31.407
Really? What book is it?

16:31.490 --> 16:34.201
Well… Here it is. This is what I wanted.

16:35.035 --> 16:36.036
The book you wanted…

16:36.787 --> 16:37.621
was "Princess"?

16:39.415 --> 16:40.874
[faint laughter]

16:43.711 --> 16:44.878
Wow.

16:44.962 --> 16:47.006
What?
You have a problem with my tastes?

16:47.089 --> 16:49.842
No, I have no prejudices.

16:51.385 --> 16:54.430
But you liked tragic love stories

16:54.513 --> 16:55.389
and sad endings?

16:55.472 --> 16:56.890
Yeah, he does.

16:57.725 --> 16:58.851
How do you know that?

16:58.934 --> 16:59.935
I just do.

17:00.686 --> 17:02.938
[sighs] A weirdo next to an oddball.

17:03.689 --> 17:06.942
You two should stick together.
You'll bother less people that way.

17:07.026 --> 17:09.903
He picks a fight as soon as he comes.
So annoying.

17:10.195 --> 17:11.071
[chuckles softly]

17:25.836 --> 17:28.005
- What should we do now?
- [Seung-hyo groans]

17:28.088 --> 17:29.923
What do you think? Let's go home.

17:30.007 --> 17:32.885
No, I have free time outside
from 8:00 p.m. to 10:00 p.m.

17:34.303 --> 17:36.305
You planned out your free time too?

17:36.388 --> 17:38.682
Old habits die hard. What a tiring life.

17:38.766 --> 17:40.225
What? What's wrong with that?

17:40.309 --> 17:43.145
I might as well have fun
in a planned and systematic way.

17:44.104 --> 17:46.315
On that note, how about some board games?

17:47.107 --> 17:49.902
Next time. I have to go home and study.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.737
Study for what?

17:51.820 --> 17:53.864
Powerboat certification.

17:54.823 --> 17:56.784
A boat license? You want drive a boat?

17:56.867 --> 18:00.037
No, I developed an interest
in something recently.

18:00.120 --> 18:01.080
But it's required.

18:01.663 --> 18:04.708
I still have work left.
I have to get back to the office.

18:04.792 --> 18:09.755
What is this?
Are you saying you're both leaving me?

18:09.838 --> 18:11.298
Is this really the end?

18:11.381 --> 18:12.674
Bye. Call me tomorrow.

18:12.758 --> 18:13.634
Don't call me.

18:13.717 --> 18:14.551
Come on.

18:15.928 --> 18:18.347
Yeah, fine! You loyal citizens.

18:18.430 --> 18:19.807
You pillars of industry!

18:19.890 --> 18:23.602
The future of Korea depends on you!
Keep up the great work!

18:24.937 --> 18:26.105
What do I do by myself?

18:32.402 --> 18:33.987
[mellow music playing]

18:41.537 --> 18:44.081
Okay. Here's your morning coffee.

18:44.164 --> 18:45.124
Thank you.

18:45.207 --> 18:47.918
Sure. There you go. It's better with that.

18:48.001 --> 18:49.002
That's right.

18:50.587 --> 18:53.340
The sweetness is really getting
my blood pumping.

18:53.423 --> 18:55.342
Don't you have a coffee machine

18:55.425 --> 18:56.385
or a pour over set?

18:56.468 --> 18:58.595
If she did,
this wouldn't be a real estate office.

18:58.679 --> 19:00.139
- My back hurts.
- [Mi-suk] Jeez.

19:00.222 --> 19:03.058
- Jae-suk, give me that cushion.
- Just take it yourself.

19:03.142 --> 19:04.184
She doesn't lift a finger.

19:04.268 --> 19:05.978
Good morning! [chuckles]

19:06.061 --> 19:08.105
- Hey.
- [Jae-suk] What's with the flowers?

19:08.188 --> 19:10.774
I bought them from a flower shop
after taking the subway.

19:10.858 --> 19:11.692
Pretty, right?

19:11.775 --> 19:12.609
- Gosh.
- They are!

19:12.693 --> 19:15.237
My husband never buys me anything
this pretty.

19:15.320 --> 19:18.615
Nor do my kids. So what can I do?
I'll buy them for others.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.492
- Thanks so much.
- [In-suk] Pretty, right?

19:20.576 --> 19:22.953
I can't remember
the last time I got flowers.

19:23.036 --> 19:25.581
- Wait, I want to take a picture.
- [Jae-suk] Sure.

19:25.664 --> 19:27.374
- Send it to me.
- They're lavenders.

19:27.457 --> 19:28.625
- [In-suk] Okay.
- So fragrant.

19:28.709 --> 19:31.086
- [Mi-suk] Move your face, Jae-suk.
- This smells so nice.

19:31.170 --> 19:32.004
[In-suk] Right?

19:32.087 --> 19:33.463
Move your face, Jae-suk.

19:33.547 --> 19:35.132
Listen while you look at these.

19:35.215 --> 19:38.010
- [Mi-suk] There!
- I have a matter to bring up.

19:38.093 --> 19:40.762
Let's change the name of our group.

19:40.846 --> 19:43.056
- Why?
- You want to change our group's name?

19:43.140 --> 19:45.726
Yeah. You remember how nasty
the Hee Sisters were?

19:45.809 --> 19:47.352
- [Jae-suk] Yeah.
- The worst.

19:47.436 --> 19:50.606
I don't want to be associated with them,
and our name doesn't help.

19:50.689 --> 19:54.109
Let's change it
to something really nice this time!

19:54.193 --> 19:55.110
Like what?

19:55.194 --> 19:56.278
You know,

19:56.361 --> 19:58.780
something refined and elegant.

19:58.864 --> 20:00.616
Should we translate Suk to English?

20:00.699 --> 20:02.492
Hye-suk, what's "suk" in English?

20:03.493 --> 20:04.328
I don't know.

20:04.411 --> 20:06.330
You're a diplomat. You don't know?

20:06.413 --> 20:08.790
- How can I know the names of plants?
- Seriously?

20:08.874 --> 20:10.709
- [Hye-suk] To ask that…
- Search on your phone.

20:10.792 --> 20:12.461
Wait. Let me search it.

20:12.544 --> 20:14.630
Wait. They don't eat it outside of Korea?

20:14.713 --> 20:16.882
- I don't think so.
- I've never heard of it.

20:17.382 --> 20:19.259
Hey, I found it.

20:19.343 --> 20:20.677
- What is it?
- Mugwort.

20:20.761 --> 20:22.596
- Mug… What?
- Mugwort.

20:22.679 --> 20:24.473
Wort. Like this.

20:24.556 --> 20:25.390
Are you barking?

20:25.474 --> 20:26.808
- It's worse.
- [Hye-suk] What?

20:26.892 --> 20:28.769
No, it doesn't roll off the tongue.

20:28.852 --> 20:31.563
But isn't mugwort a type of herb too?

20:31.647 --> 20:32.731
- Yeah.
- [Mi-suk] Yeah.

20:32.814 --> 20:34.316
And what's the ultimate herb?

20:34.399 --> 20:36.318
Lavender!

20:36.401 --> 20:37.486
You have to be quick!

20:37.569 --> 20:39.112
It's settled! Lavender.

20:39.196 --> 20:41.240
NA MI-SUK
LIVE WITH FRAGRANCE

20:41.365 --> 20:43.116
- Hey, Dad?
- [Geun-sik] Yeah?

20:43.200 --> 20:45.619
How do you live with fragrance?

20:45.702 --> 20:48.622
I don't know. [chuckles]
Ask your mom when she gets here.

20:48.705 --> 20:50.916
She must be getting old. Take a look.

20:51.250 --> 20:53.502
She put flowers as her profile picture.

20:53.627 --> 20:56.838
- [Geun-sik] Lavenders.
- Saying your mom's old behind her back?

20:57.631 --> 21:00.092
This is why I can't leave you two alone.

21:00.175 --> 21:01.093
You're so violent.

21:01.176 --> 21:03.387
I wasn't talking behind your back.
I just stated a fact.

21:03.470 --> 21:05.138
We're growing old together.

21:05.222 --> 21:07.057
Just keep quiet.

21:07.140 --> 21:08.850
Why are you making so many?

21:08.934 --> 21:10.978
We still have a way to go.
We need to make 100.

21:11.103 --> 21:12.771
- A hundred?
- [Geun-sik] Yeah.

21:12.854 --> 21:15.107
A TV production crew came
and bought them before.

21:15.190 --> 21:16.566
They liked them and ordered again.

21:17.150 --> 21:18.151
Really?

21:18.235 --> 21:19.569
I guess I have no choice.

21:19.653 --> 21:20.612
I should help out.

21:20.696 --> 21:21.905
[Mi-suk] Hey!

21:21.989 --> 21:23.865
Forget it. What can you do?

21:23.949 --> 21:26.201
Don't get in the way.
Just eat some kimbap.

21:26.285 --> 21:27.369
Or have tteokbokki.

21:27.452 --> 21:29.204
- Do you want some?
- No, you're busy.

21:29.288 --> 21:30.789
- [bell chiming]
- Welcome…

21:30.872 --> 21:32.040
- [Mi-suk] Welcome!
- Hello.

21:32.124 --> 21:33.375
Ms. Yu!

21:34.293 --> 21:37.129
[gasps] Goodness. Is that you, Seok-ryu?

21:37.212 --> 21:40.048
Wow! You haven't changed at all.

21:40.132 --> 21:43.719
I knew it was you
as soon as you walked in. Wow!

21:43.802 --> 21:46.596
Mom, my homeroom teacher from high school.

21:46.680 --> 21:48.432
- Goodness!
- Hello, Ms. Yu!

21:49.391 --> 21:51.727
I'm so sorry I didn't recognize you.

21:51.810 --> 21:52.978
No, it's fine.

21:53.061 --> 21:57.524
I only realized after seeing Seok-ryu.
I forgot her parents ran this shop.

21:57.607 --> 21:59.276
What brings you here?

21:59.359 --> 22:01.028
I came to order food.

22:01.111 --> 22:04.489
Can I get 20 orders of tteokbokki
and 20 orders of sundae?

22:04.573 --> 22:05.741
- Of course.
- Goodness.

22:05.824 --> 22:07.242
We'd be so grateful.

22:07.326 --> 22:09.995
But it's so much.
Can you take them by yourself?

22:10.078 --> 22:12.539
- [Geun-sik] I'll help her.
- No, I'll go. You're busy.

22:12.622 --> 22:14.166
- You will?
- Just a moment.

22:14.249 --> 22:15.167
- Okay.
- [Mi-suk] Honey.

22:15.250 --> 22:16.418
- I'll do that.
- Just a moment.

22:16.501 --> 22:18.587
- [Geun-sik] Hurry.
- [Mi-suk] Hey. Get Ms. Yu a drink.

22:19.171 --> 22:21.673
Thanks for delivering this for me.

22:21.757 --> 22:23.592
Of course.

22:23.675 --> 22:24.843
[Jin-ae chuckles]

22:24.926 --> 22:28.347
Wow, the school hasn't changed at all.

22:29.306 --> 22:31.558
It's always the same here.

22:32.309 --> 22:35.937
Maybe that's why I keep forgetting
that time's passing. [chuckles softly]

22:36.021 --> 22:40.150
It's amazing. I can't believe
you're the principal now. [gasps]

22:40.233 --> 22:41.068
You too.

22:42.110 --> 22:46.031
You were so childish.
I can't believe you're all grown up now.

22:46.114 --> 22:48.784
Are you visiting Korea
for a short while? A vacation?

22:48.867 --> 22:49.701
What?

22:50.243 --> 22:52.037
I heard you work at Greip.

22:52.120 --> 22:53.663
Yeah…

22:53.747 --> 22:57.250
I was so happy when I heard that.

22:57.334 --> 22:58.668
And I wasn't the only one.

22:58.752 --> 23:00.879
All the teachers still talk about you.

23:00.962 --> 23:02.547
You were so capable and smart.

23:02.631 --> 23:05.884
A renowned figure
of Hyereung High School. [chuckles]

23:07.385 --> 23:10.388
Look, another renowned figure
of Hyereung High School.

23:10.472 --> 23:11.598
[indistinct chatter]

23:12.933 --> 23:13.850
[Seok-ryu] What?

23:20.982 --> 23:25.237
You applied for the gym remodeling
and new building design competition?

23:25.320 --> 23:28.490
Yeah, today's the site briefing
for the participating companies.

23:28.573 --> 23:31.785
[Jin-ae] I had my doubts
when I saw a familiar name on the list.

23:31.868 --> 23:35.247
This is great.
It would mean so much if you did it.

23:36.665 --> 23:37.666
Ms. Yu.

23:37.749 --> 23:42.003
Doesn't that mean he shouldn't
be sitting here with you right now?

23:42.087 --> 23:44.089
He technically has academic ties.

23:44.172 --> 23:45.382
It violates fairness.

23:45.465 --> 23:46.550
[laughs]

23:46.633 --> 23:47.843
You haven't changed.

23:48.426 --> 23:52.264
Experts from the education department
will do the evaluations.

23:52.347 --> 23:53.765
I have no authority.

23:54.307 --> 23:55.725
Nice try.

23:56.351 --> 23:57.435
Rats.

23:57.519 --> 24:00.230
It's been so long.
Are you free this afternoon?

24:00.313 --> 24:01.731
Of course.

24:01.815 --> 24:02.649
I'm sorry.

24:02.732 --> 24:06.027
I missed a few things
from the site visit earlier.

24:06.111 --> 24:07.737
I need to look more thoroughly.

24:07.821 --> 24:11.074
Is that so? That's too bad.
I'll have to ask Seok-ryu then.

24:11.158 --> 24:13.160
Since you're here, talk to the students.

24:13.618 --> 24:15.203
A chat with an alumnus.

24:15.287 --> 24:18.123
Excuse me? Me?

24:18.206 --> 24:21.084
I think you'll set a good example.

24:21.168 --> 24:24.629
I bet the students will be excited
to hear you work at Greip.

24:25.380 --> 24:27.424
But I…

24:27.507 --> 24:29.384
I'll get going then.

24:29.467 --> 24:32.429
[Jin-ae] Okay, I know you're busy.
Thanks. I'll wish you luck.

24:32.512 --> 24:33.346
Thank you.

24:34.139 --> 24:36.141
Are you okay with meeting the students?

24:36.224 --> 24:38.351
Sure.

24:40.312 --> 24:44.983
This is Bae Seok-ryu.
She's a graduate of our school.

24:45.066 --> 24:47.819
- She works at Greip in the US.
- [all gasping]

24:47.903 --> 24:49.196
- Greip?
- That's cool!

24:50.071 --> 24:52.490
I hope her energy rubs off on you.

24:52.574 --> 24:54.701
This old boomer will leave,
so talk freely.

24:54.784 --> 24:56.119
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

24:56.203 --> 24:57.329
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

25:01.958 --> 25:04.211
Hello, I'm Bae Seok-ryu.

25:04.294 --> 25:05.295
[all cheering]

25:07.047 --> 25:09.925
This was actually came together
very suddenly,

25:10.008 --> 25:11.801
so I didn't prepare anything.

25:12.385 --> 25:15.263
You can ask me questions if you want.
I'll answer them.

25:15.764 --> 25:16.973
What college did you go to?

25:17.057 --> 25:20.977
I got accepted to Hanguk University
after I graduated high school.

25:21.061 --> 25:23.980
After attending for a year,
I studied abroad in the US.

25:24.064 --> 25:27.400
I enrolled at UC Berkkeley and graduated.

25:28.235 --> 25:30.237
Does that mean your family's rich?

25:30.320 --> 25:32.447
Not at all.

25:32.530 --> 25:34.783
A friend was preparing to study abroad.

25:34.866 --> 25:37.911
I wanted to study English too,
so we prepared together.

25:37.994 --> 25:39.496
After I was accepted,

25:39.579 --> 25:42.499
I received a scholarship for four years.
That's how I went.

25:43.416 --> 25:44.834
- That's nuts.
- Wow.

25:44.918 --> 25:45.961
- Wait…
- [Seok-ryu] Yes?

25:46.044 --> 25:47.545
What do you do at Greip?

25:47.629 --> 25:49.881
It's called a product manager.

25:49.965 --> 25:53.426
I'm responsible for overseeing
and managing projects

25:53.510 --> 25:56.263
from their planning stage
to the end result.

25:56.346 --> 26:01.184
Was being a product manager
always your dream?

26:02.560 --> 26:06.022
I don't know. I don't think so.

26:06.106 --> 26:07.649
Then, what was your dream?

26:08.483 --> 26:09.859
- My dream?
- Yes.

26:09.943 --> 26:13.280
When you were in high school,
what did you want to be?

26:16.032 --> 26:17.367
[mellow music playing]

26:31.339 --> 26:32.299
[water splashing]

26:34.175 --> 26:35.635
[water dripping]

26:52.444 --> 26:54.237
[Seung-hyo] Hey, Seok-ryu.

26:55.572 --> 26:58.199
There you go ignoring me again.
Have you had lunch?

26:58.283 --> 27:00.785
Don't talk to me. I want peace and quiet.

27:00.869 --> 27:02.454
Then, quietly come with me.

27:03.121 --> 27:03.955
Later.

27:04.622 --> 27:05.790
We have to go now.

27:05.874 --> 27:07.834
Says who? I don't want to go.

27:08.626 --> 27:10.545
Come with me!

27:11.087 --> 27:13.757
Are you insane?
How dare you grab a woman by the neck?

27:13.840 --> 27:15.467
How could you be so thoughtless?

27:15.550 --> 27:17.344
Speak for yourself. Are you insane?

27:17.427 --> 27:19.095
You're no woman.

27:19.179 --> 27:20.805
Of course, I'm a woman.

27:20.889 --> 27:23.099
Am I a man? What am I then?

27:23.933 --> 27:24.934
You are…

27:26.269 --> 27:27.562
almost gender neutral.

27:27.645 --> 27:29.022
Do you want to die today?

27:29.522 --> 27:32.359
- You want to be buried behind the school?
- Let's go then.

27:34.027 --> 27:35.487
- What?
- Let's go.

27:38.740 --> 27:39.908
[quirky music playing]

27:41.951 --> 27:43.953
I'm sure it was around here.

27:44.788 --> 27:46.748
You've been saying that for 30 minutes.

27:47.624 --> 27:49.376
Why are we looking for this?

27:49.459 --> 27:53.505
We agreed to take it out after ten years.
It's way past that deadline.

27:53.588 --> 27:55.298
I know.

27:55.382 --> 27:58.802
We forgot about that time capsule.
What's so important about it?

27:58.885 --> 28:01.221
I don't even remember what I put in there.

28:01.304 --> 28:03.473
Hey, you're the one who wanted to do it.

28:03.556 --> 28:07.394
I think it was a letter.
"A letter to me in ten years."

28:07.936 --> 28:11.773
I must've been crazy.
That millennial sentiment is awful.

28:12.399 --> 28:16.152
Forget it. Don't look for it.
Let's keep it deep in there.

28:16.236 --> 28:19.823
Let's hope it's found a billion years
from now like a dinosaur egg!

28:19.906 --> 28:21.491
No, it'd still be embarrassing.

28:21.574 --> 28:25.120
The Seok-ryu I know would let curiosity
overcome her embarrassment.

28:26.079 --> 28:27.580
Aren't you curious about it?

28:27.664 --> 28:31.501
I'm sure it's full
of dazzling and innocent words.

28:32.335 --> 28:36.256
But so what? The reality is
we're just digging really hard.

28:36.339 --> 28:40.468
Hey, anyone can tell
that you're digging half-heartedly.

28:42.762 --> 28:45.014
[exhales] It was around here.

28:47.058 --> 28:48.476
Why did you do that earlier?

28:49.310 --> 28:50.186
Do what?

28:50.812 --> 28:52.689
I acted like I still worked at Greip.

28:54.315 --> 28:55.942
Why did you play dumb too?

28:56.526 --> 28:58.403
I shamelessly gave a lecture too.

28:58.486 --> 28:59.612
You did work at Greip.

29:00.780 --> 29:01.781
Was that a sham too?

29:01.865 --> 29:03.366
Shut up.

29:03.450 --> 29:07.328
That's good enough.
Your experience there was real.

29:07.996 --> 29:10.665
I think that's enough
to give the kids good advice.

29:16.755 --> 29:17.714
[rubbing hands]

29:19.507 --> 29:21.551
Why won't this dirt come off?

29:22.135 --> 29:24.804
Stop pretending to be clean.
Just wash it off later.

29:24.888 --> 29:26.598
[rubbing hands] I want to go home.

29:26.681 --> 29:29.392
Hey, let's dig a little more.
I have a good feeling.

29:29.476 --> 29:32.228
We're almost there.
I think it was between these trees.

29:32.312 --> 29:33.521
You look for it.

29:34.606 --> 29:35.690
Are you really going?

29:36.649 --> 29:37.776
Seok-ryu!

29:38.985 --> 29:41.404
Damn. I'm sure it was between these trees.

29:42.238 --> 29:43.615
[rubbing hands]

29:47.160 --> 29:48.703
Seok-ryu, wait for me.

29:49.412 --> 29:50.538
We were almost there.

29:50.622 --> 29:51.831
[mellow music playing]

29:51.915 --> 29:52.874
Hey, Seok-ryu!

30:00.799 --> 30:02.133
I'm home.

30:02.217 --> 30:04.010
Hey!

30:07.180 --> 30:08.139
What's all of this?

30:08.890 --> 30:10.391
Gift boxes.

30:11.684 --> 30:15.104
It's the neighbor's side job,
I asked for some.

30:15.855 --> 30:17.398
Why would you do this?

30:17.482 --> 30:20.235
What's wrong with your hand?
What's with the pain relief patch?

30:20.318 --> 30:23.404
I think it was all the kimbap.
My wrist hurts.

30:23.488 --> 30:25.573
I said I'd help.

30:25.657 --> 30:28.618
You help by doing nothing,
you little brat.

30:28.701 --> 30:31.079
I can put 100 more of these patches on.

30:31.663 --> 30:34.207
I hope I can sell 1,000
or 10,000 more kimbap.

30:34.290 --> 30:36.668
- Give it. I'll do it.
- Why would you do this?

30:37.418 --> 30:38.837
This is my work.

30:38.920 --> 30:41.965
Don't interfere with my pocket money.
Go do your work.

30:43.341 --> 30:44.676
Hey, Dong-jin!

30:44.801 --> 30:46.511
She's going nuts again.

30:46.594 --> 30:48.888
You could've helped Mom
if you were at home!

30:48.972 --> 30:51.307
What do you do all day in your room?

30:51.391 --> 30:52.392
What's with you?

30:52.517 --> 30:54.936
I went to work today
and came for my stuff.

30:55.603 --> 30:57.063
- Mom!
- [Mi-suk] Yeah?

30:57.146 --> 30:58.690
I have a private lesson. I'll be late.

30:58.773 --> 30:59.858
Okay, have a good one.

31:00.441 --> 31:01.609
- I'm off.
- [Mi-suk] Bye.

31:04.696 --> 31:07.365
Dong-jin has his act together lately.

31:08.783 --> 31:11.578
I didn't think
he'd do anything with his life.

31:11.703 --> 31:13.872
He's living like a human being now.

31:13.955 --> 31:16.457
It's a part-time job, but he gets paid.

31:16.583 --> 31:19.419
The gym owner's helping him
become a personal trainer or whatever.

31:19.502 --> 31:21.254
And he's exercising.

31:24.549 --> 31:25.508
That's good.

31:26.718 --> 31:28.177
[mellow music playing]

31:30.513 --> 31:31.598
[game sounds playing]

31:36.394 --> 31:37.270
[sighs]

31:44.986 --> 31:45.820
[exhales]

31:48.907 --> 31:50.617
Can I really keep doing this?

31:54.913 --> 31:57.749
- [knock on door]
- [Myeong-u] Aren't you going home?

31:57.832 --> 31:58.666
A little later.

31:59.208 --> 32:00.209
What are you doing?

32:01.336 --> 32:04.130
Is this where you used to swim?

32:04.213 --> 32:05.256
[Seung-hyo] Yeah.

32:05.340 --> 32:06.841
It is pretty old.

32:07.759 --> 32:09.177
Is it still used today?

32:09.260 --> 32:11.804
Sometimes, during PE class.

32:13.723 --> 32:17.852
Take it easy. You know public facilities
don't make money and are full of red tape.

32:18.811 --> 32:22.231
Tomorrow's client meeting
is what's important to us right now.

32:23.316 --> 32:24.484
They're both important.

32:25.860 --> 32:30.073
It may seem like you have a reputation
and we're doing well on the outside,

32:30.156 --> 32:32.575
but you know this industry
isn't that easy.

32:32.659 --> 32:36.079
A slight downturn
can even affect major corporations.

32:36.162 --> 32:36.996
I know.

32:38.039 --> 32:42.585
So turn off the pool,
and turn on the retirement community.

32:44.796 --> 32:45.922
Are you pressuring me?

32:46.547 --> 32:48.633
No, suggesting.

32:48.716 --> 32:49.592
[chuckles softly]

32:50.093 --> 32:53.304
Also, our interview article for
The Chungwoo Daily was published.

32:53.388 --> 32:54.889
It'll be in the paper tomorrow. Bye.

32:54.973 --> 32:56.099
Bye.

33:05.358 --> 33:08.903
BUILDING ARCHITECTURE AND PEOPLE
ATELIER IN'S CHOI SEUNG-HYO, YOON MYEONG-U

33:08.987 --> 33:11.072
CHOI SEUNG-HYO WINS 200M FREESTYLE

33:11.155 --> 33:13.157
AT 2007 SEOUL NATIONAL
SWIMMING CHAMPIONSHIPS

33:17.036 --> 33:18.162
You scared me.

33:18.955 --> 33:20.456
Why are you standing there?

33:21.040 --> 33:24.877
This is why there are so many
strange rumors about you at work.

33:24.961 --> 33:28.297
They say you have spiritual energy
or a third eye on your forehead.

33:28.381 --> 33:31.759
That I have a spiritual eye
and can see through people.

33:31.843 --> 33:33.011
[laughs]

33:33.553 --> 33:35.555
I'm just farsighted due to old age.

33:37.306 --> 33:39.767
How's the article? Do you hate it?

33:39.851 --> 33:41.519
It's not bad.

33:41.602 --> 33:43.771
The concept's good
and the content's clear.

33:44.313 --> 33:46.441
So why doesn't it sound like a compliment?

33:49.027 --> 33:50.236
You're getting sluggish.

33:50.820 --> 33:53.031
Your writing shows
that there was no legwork.

33:53.114 --> 33:54.991
Kang Dan-ho.

33:55.491 --> 33:59.287
I thought you were a madman
when you first joined the company.

34:00.246 --> 34:02.123
When you went around police stations,

34:02.206 --> 34:04.959
you'd pack a backpack
and wouldn't come home for months.

34:05.585 --> 34:08.880
So what? Am I too focused
on maintaining a work-life balance now?

34:09.922 --> 34:11.257
I get it. I really do.

34:12.425 --> 34:13.634
Let's be more proactive.

34:14.552 --> 34:15.887
I'll keep that in mind.

34:17.221 --> 34:20.683
- Are you putting it into action now?
- No, I'm going to buy rice cakes.

34:24.979 --> 34:25.813
[sighs]

34:27.648 --> 34:28.483
Not bad.

34:29.025 --> 34:30.068
[tires screech]

34:30.151 --> 34:31.611
[suspenseful music playing]

34:31.694 --> 34:33.905
- [Mo-eum] Where's the patient?
- [teacher] Over there.

34:43.706 --> 34:45.541
[Mo-eum] When did his seizure start?

34:45.625 --> 34:47.210
About ten or 15 minutes ago.

34:47.877 --> 34:50.088
Do-hyeon suffers from status seizures.

34:50.171 --> 34:52.006
Let's move him. Mo-eum, sit up front.

34:52.090 --> 34:53.174
[Mo-eum] Okay.

34:53.758 --> 34:54.634
Just a second.

34:54.717 --> 34:55.843
[siren blaring]

35:01.516 --> 35:03.267
What do we do? The road is blocked.

35:04.977 --> 35:06.979
We're transporting an emergency patient.

35:07.063 --> 35:10.483
We're transporting an emergency patient.
Please cooperate.

35:11.442 --> 35:14.529
[Min-ho] A seizure
over 20 minutes is dangerous.

35:14.612 --> 35:16.030
Why aren't we moving?

35:17.240 --> 35:19.575
We have a sick kid. Please, move.

35:23.704 --> 35:25.039
What's that person doing?

35:26.290 --> 35:29.335
I think he's trying to clear a path!

35:30.545 --> 35:31.379
What?

35:31.462 --> 35:33.339
I LOVE YOU, MUDFLATS

35:33.422 --> 35:34.799
MUDFLAT GUARDIAN

35:34.882 --> 35:35.842
[siren blaring]

35:48.563 --> 35:49.397
[scoffs]

35:52.650 --> 35:54.068
[Jeong-u] Okay, that's good.

36:09.542 --> 36:11.294
I LOVE YOU, MUDFLATS

36:27.935 --> 36:31.105
A lot of retirement communities
have been popping up lately,

36:31.189 --> 36:33.566
but the quality varies widely, doesn't it?

36:33.649 --> 36:37.486
Thus, our cheapest unit will start
at two billion won for the deposit.

36:37.570 --> 36:40.031
We plan to build
a luxurious retirement community.

36:40.114 --> 36:44.744
The facility will be designed exclusively
for the top 1% of the senior population.

36:45.328 --> 36:49.540
It'll be as beautiful as a landmark since
it'll be located in the heart of Seoul.

36:49.624 --> 36:53.169
It'll be a place that not just anyone
can have access to or even look at.

36:53.252 --> 36:56.339
For example, the elderly who ride
the subway for free.

36:57.423 --> 36:59.258
I love the subway.

36:59.342 --> 37:01.344
I drove my car today,

37:01.427 --> 37:03.804
but I ride it often
when I have to travel a lot.

37:03.888 --> 37:05.514
I'll enjoy it in the future too.

37:05.598 --> 37:09.018
I'm in favor of welfare policies
that provide transportation benefits

37:09.101 --> 37:10.228
to the elderly.

37:10.311 --> 37:12.104
[Myeong-u chuckles nervously]

37:12.980 --> 37:13.898
That's great.

37:13.981 --> 37:15.691
[both laughing]

37:15.775 --> 37:18.819
We weren't trying to be demeaning.

37:18.903 --> 37:20.446
It was just a comparison.

37:20.529 --> 37:22.198
- Yes, of course.
- Right.

37:22.281 --> 37:25.785
But if it's going to be at a level
where people can't even look at it,

37:25.868 --> 37:28.037
how high are you planning to build it?

37:28.621 --> 37:29.956
People's necks will hurt.

37:30.873 --> 37:33.709
[Myeong-u] Well,
what Mr. Choi is trying to say

37:33.793 --> 37:37.713
is what kind of concept
are you looking for?

37:37.797 --> 37:41.592
Are you thinking of something
luxurious and extravagant?

37:41.676 --> 37:45.763
Yes, that's why we prepared some drafts.

37:46.514 --> 37:48.975
I'd like to mix in some of these designs.

37:49.767 --> 37:50.601
Excuse me?

37:50.685 --> 37:53.562
As you can see, these are works
by renowned international designers.

37:54.188 --> 37:58.276
Our potential clients have spent
a lot of time overseas before.

37:58.359 --> 38:00.486
Their tastes and standards are quite high.

38:00.569 --> 38:04.407
So, ordinary domestic designs
won't be able to satisfy them.

38:04.490 --> 38:06.867
So you're saying…

38:07.952 --> 38:09.787
you don't trust our capabilities

38:10.371 --> 38:12.915
and want us to replicate
verified designs, right?

38:12.999 --> 38:14.583
Is that what you're requesting?

38:14.667 --> 38:16.002
Excuse me, Mr. Choi?

38:16.085 --> 38:17.503
[Hong-jin] It's an homage.

38:17.586 --> 38:19.422
All artistic creation
is a form of imitation.

38:19.505 --> 38:21.132
Nothing's ever really new.

38:21.215 --> 38:24.010
No, this is clearly plagiarism.

38:24.093 --> 38:26.512
[Kyu-hyung] You don't have
to worry about that.

38:26.595 --> 38:28.639
Everyone cries about plagiarism lately.

38:29.223 --> 38:32.768
But when it's debated in court,
it's difficult to enforce penalties.

38:35.354 --> 38:36.522
I can't do this.

38:37.231 --> 38:38.941
Don't try to talk me into it.

38:39.025 --> 38:40.693
I'll never change my mind.

38:40.776 --> 38:44.113
Just hear me out first. I have a plan too.

38:44.196 --> 38:45.156
What plan?

38:45.239 --> 38:47.283
First, we pretend to play along.

38:47.366 --> 38:49.994
Then, we change the design as we proceed.

38:50.077 --> 38:51.495
We offer a new design.

38:52.079 --> 38:54.206
Come on. The dates and budget are all set.

38:54.290 --> 38:56.792
They can't stop midway either.

38:56.876 --> 38:59.712
We'll gradually make changes
and integrate our style.

38:59.795 --> 39:00.755
Sounds good, right?

39:00.838 --> 39:03.799
So you want to retouch
a plagiarized design!

39:04.967 --> 39:06.594
Think of it as a reference.

39:06.677 --> 39:07.720
Are you joking?

39:08.220 --> 39:09.221
Myeong-u.

39:09.847 --> 39:13.184
I know that architecture can't be done
without a client,

39:14.226 --> 39:16.896
I can't work with people
who have that mindset.

39:20.733 --> 39:24.737
With that kind of attitude,
we won't be able to do anything.

39:24.862 --> 39:28.240
We'll have to deal with all sorts
of dirty, disgraceful things.

39:28.324 --> 39:29.492
Is this how you'll act?

39:30.034 --> 39:33.954
We built our office on a mountain of debt.
We have employees to take care of.

39:34.038 --> 39:35.790
For their sake, I won't do it.

39:36.707 --> 39:39.168
I want to preserve their pride
as architects.

39:39.251 --> 39:42.671
You fool!
Do you know what they really need?

39:42.755 --> 39:44.799
They don't need this abstract sentiment.

39:44.882 --> 39:47.718
They need practical incentives.
Salary increases!

39:48.469 --> 39:51.347
- If we want to do that, we need money.
- [Seung-hyo sighs]

39:51.430 --> 39:53.140
The company must do well.

39:54.350 --> 39:57.019
So you want to sell your soul for money?

39:57.478 --> 39:59.772
Is that really what's best
for our company?

39:59.855 --> 40:01.190
Then, what about you?

40:01.273 --> 40:03.275
Are you doing anything for the company?

40:03.776 --> 40:06.112
You didn't care
about the retirement community!

40:06.195 --> 40:08.489
- You're always looking at that pool!
- What?

40:08.572 --> 40:12.451
A retirement community worth hundreds
of billions and a simple gym renovation!

40:12.535 --> 40:14.578
One can't even compare with the other!

40:14.662 --> 40:16.789
You brought personal feelings into work!

40:17.331 --> 40:18.499
Myeong-u.

40:18.582 --> 40:20.626
That damn pool reminded you of the past…

40:23.754 --> 40:24.588
[groans]

40:26.715 --> 40:29.510
I mean… Look, Seung-hyo…

40:33.222 --> 40:34.473
I'm heading out.

40:35.307 --> 40:36.142
Wait…

40:41.439 --> 40:42.273
[sighs]

40:44.525 --> 40:45.818
[Min-ho] Great job.

40:45.901 --> 40:46.944
Great work.

40:47.027 --> 40:48.779
[Jeong-u] Great work!

40:48.863 --> 40:52.366
I'm glad Do-hyeon is doing better.

40:52.450 --> 40:54.702
This is all thanks to you, Mr. Yeon.

40:54.785 --> 40:55.661
[exclaims]

40:55.744 --> 40:57.246
It's my area of expertise.

40:57.329 --> 41:00.458
When Se-yoon was first diagnosed
with epilepsy,

41:01.250 --> 41:03.002
I thought my world was ending.

41:03.085 --> 41:07.298
I guess it was a task given by the heavens
to turn us into better paramedics.

41:07.381 --> 41:10.759
- Se-yoon's a gift from the heavens.
- Of course.

41:10.843 --> 41:11.760
[both chuckle]

41:11.844 --> 41:14.346
Who's the savior
that cleared the road for us?

41:14.430 --> 41:16.140
- My ideal type.
- [Jeong-u] What?

41:16.223 --> 41:19.852
I usually preferred people
who were like action stars.

41:19.935 --> 41:21.812
But not anymore.

41:22.480 --> 41:24.690
I like someone
who's stoic but full of drive.

41:24.773 --> 41:26.358
The silent but determined type.

41:26.442 --> 41:29.737
Wow. That's what's really sexy.

41:29.820 --> 41:33.866
It's the first time she's describing
someone who's not Iron Man as sexy.

41:33.949 --> 41:35.910
No, she said Spider-Man was sexy too.

41:35.993 --> 41:37.661
The muscles through the tights…

41:37.745 --> 41:40.206
What did it say on the back of his shirt?
Mud something?

41:40.289 --> 41:41.290
"I love you, mudflats."

41:41.373 --> 41:42.958
- Yeah, that's right.
- [Min-ho chuckles]

41:43.042 --> 41:47.922
That means he's Mudflat Man.
Iron Man, Spider-Man, Mudflat Man.

41:49.006 --> 41:50.174
Mudflat Man.

41:51.800 --> 41:55.012
Did anyone see
Mudflat Man's license plate number?

41:55.095 --> 41:58.224
Sorry. I should've checked.
Things were so hectic.

41:58.307 --> 42:02.102
You should've checked.
How will I find him now?

42:02.186 --> 42:05.648
Ms. Jung, this came for you.

42:05.731 --> 42:08.275
I see. Thank you so much.

42:08.359 --> 42:10.277
- What is this?
- What is it?

42:11.987 --> 42:14.240
[Min-ho] Rice cakes? I was getting hungry.

42:14.323 --> 42:15.407
Can we eat some?

42:15.491 --> 42:18.244
Just a second.
Let's see who sent them first.

42:18.327 --> 42:19.328
[Jeong-u] Here it is.

42:19.411 --> 42:21.038
- There's a card.
- [Mo-eum] There it is.

42:21.121 --> 42:21.956
[Jeong-u] Okay.

42:22.039 --> 42:24.166
Come on. Wait.

42:25.167 --> 42:27.253
[Dan-ho] Thank you so much for last time.

42:27.836 --> 42:32.258
I promised I'd reach out, didn't I?
Paramedic Jung Mo-eum.

42:32.341 --> 42:33.926
What?

42:34.969 --> 42:37.137
How did he know my name?

42:39.431 --> 42:40.808
[both] Mmm.

42:40.891 --> 42:43.769
But why did he have to send rice cakes?
It's making me thirsty.

42:44.895 --> 42:45.729
Give me some.

42:47.606 --> 42:48.440
It's good.

42:49.024 --> 42:50.859
[jazz music playing in background]

42:51.819 --> 42:53.779
- [Jin-young] Ms. Bae Seok-ryu?
- Ah.

42:55.573 --> 42:57.449
- Hello.
- Hello.

42:57.533 --> 43:00.369
It's nice to meet you. I'm Lee Jin-young.

43:00.452 --> 43:01.287
Thank you.

43:01.370 --> 43:03.330
[Jin-young] Were you surprised by my call?

43:03.414 --> 43:04.373
Not at all.

43:07.126 --> 43:10.629
I could've come to meet you.
Thank you for coming to my neighborhood.

43:10.713 --> 43:12.047
It was nothing.

43:12.631 --> 43:15.092
I should come to meet someone
as esteemed as you.

43:15.175 --> 43:16.176
[chuckles softly]

43:16.927 --> 43:19.346
But how did you get my number?

43:19.430 --> 43:22.141
I've got a great radar.

43:23.100 --> 43:25.686
I heard a talented person
came back to Korea,

43:25.769 --> 43:27.146
so I started to ask around.

43:27.229 --> 43:29.398
You flatter me. Thank you.

43:29.481 --> 43:30.858
[Jin-young] I mean it.

43:30.941 --> 43:32.234
If you don't mind,

43:33.235 --> 43:36.864
may I ask you why you quit Greip

43:36.947 --> 43:38.240
and came back like this?

43:38.324 --> 43:43.162
I had a personal reason to come home.

43:43.245 --> 43:44.121
I see.

43:45.205 --> 43:47.541
Then, how long did you work at Greip?

43:48.125 --> 43:50.586
I joined the company in 2015,

43:50.669 --> 43:53.464
and I officially quit last month.

43:54.298 --> 43:55.758
[Jin-young] So ten years?

43:56.508 --> 43:59.845
No, I took a year off in the middle.

44:00.846 --> 44:01.847
[Jin-young] You did?

44:01.930 --> 44:03.641
Yes, when I was 30.

44:03.724 --> 44:05.392
Was that for personal reasons as well?

44:05.976 --> 44:06.894
Yes.

44:07.895 --> 44:09.188
Being 30 is like that.

44:10.022 --> 44:12.149
I transferred jobs at that age.

44:12.983 --> 44:15.361
Your career and portfolio
are very impressive.

44:15.444 --> 44:17.154
I don't think it'll be a problem.

44:17.863 --> 44:21.408
The position I want to offer
is at Serendipity…

44:29.583 --> 44:31.835
[clicks tongue, sighs]

44:43.305 --> 44:44.223
Bae Seok-ryu.

44:46.266 --> 44:47.810
Why are you dressed like that?

44:47.893 --> 44:48.936
What's this?

44:49.853 --> 44:51.730
Why do you keep showing up like this?

44:51.814 --> 44:54.149
Because we live in the same neighborhood.

44:54.233 --> 44:55.567
I'm not happy about it either.

44:55.651 --> 44:57.444
Looks like we're on the same page.

44:57.861 --> 44:58.904
Just be on your way.

45:00.280 --> 45:01.281
Where are you going?

45:01.365 --> 45:03.283
To wake up and smell the coffee.

45:04.701 --> 45:05.536
[sighs]

45:10.958 --> 45:11.792
[slurping]

45:13.794 --> 45:16.505
- [exclaims]
- How have you become even more carefree?

45:16.588 --> 45:17.673
You sure are bold.

45:18.632 --> 45:20.259
- Want some?
- You drank from that.

45:20.342 --> 45:22.094
- At least rinse it.
- You think I'm dirty?

45:22.177 --> 45:23.137
You don't look clean.

45:23.846 --> 45:24.888
- Come on.
- Sorry.

45:24.972 --> 45:25.889
[Seung-hyo] Seriously?

45:25.973 --> 45:28.600
- Did you spray water on me?
- No, my hand slipped.

45:29.518 --> 45:30.394
Just you wait.

45:30.936 --> 45:33.397
To spray on me?
Our country has a water shortage.

45:34.982 --> 45:36.233
This is for the Earth.

45:39.153 --> 45:40.195
[slurping]

45:43.991 --> 45:45.200
Where are you going now?

45:50.289 --> 45:53.292
Why are you so unpredictable in everything
that you do?

45:54.668 --> 45:56.920
I've lost muscle mass
lying around all day.

45:57.004 --> 45:58.130
I have to regain it.

45:58.213 --> 46:00.132
Do you have any muscle mass to lose?

46:00.215 --> 46:02.259
You also never dress right
for any occasion.

46:02.342 --> 46:04.136
It was right until now.

46:04.219 --> 46:05.971
I met with a job recruiter earlier.

46:08.182 --> 46:09.892
- Why?
- [Seok-ryu] I don't know.

46:09.975 --> 46:11.727
I don't know how she got my number.

46:12.728 --> 46:15.230
But you know how capable
and talented I am.

46:15.856 --> 46:17.566
What did she say?

46:17.649 --> 46:19.276
She offered me a few positions.

46:19.359 --> 46:21.653
GLO Korea and Serendipity.

46:22.488 --> 46:24.615
The conditions were pretty good.

46:25.449 --> 46:28.452
It's not as much as before,
but the pay is decent too.

46:29.161 --> 46:29.995
Really?

46:30.078 --> 46:32.122
It's similar to the work I did before.

46:32.915 --> 46:34.082
I'll adjust quickly.

46:34.917 --> 46:35.792
Great, right?

46:37.211 --> 46:38.420
Do you want to do it?

46:40.005 --> 46:42.424
- What?
- You want to do that kind of work again?

46:42.508 --> 46:44.843
Work is just work.

46:44.968 --> 46:47.554
- Does it matter if I want to do it or not?
- That's not right.

46:47.679 --> 46:50.098
It's your work,
so you should do what you want.

46:50.182 --> 46:53.519
How can people only do
what they want to do?

46:53.602 --> 46:54.645
Why not?

46:55.395 --> 46:58.023
Why does everyone compromise with reality?

46:58.857 --> 47:01.360
You said you overheated and shut down.

47:02.236 --> 47:04.571
- You said you wanted to reboot.
- Yeah, but…

47:04.655 --> 47:07.199
This is the courage you mustered?
Returning to your old life?

47:07.282 --> 47:11.370
- So what if I do? What's it to you?
- You think I don't know you?

47:11.495 --> 47:14.164
When you want to do something,
your eyes light up

47:14.248 --> 47:17.209
and stomp with excitement,
but I don't see any of that now.

47:17.292 --> 47:20.587
Do I still look like a teenager to you?

47:20.671 --> 47:23.006
Don't act like you know me
because we were friends as kids.

47:23.090 --> 47:25.842
I just wish you'd find your real dream.

47:25.926 --> 47:27.761
Dream? Hey! Dreams?

47:27.844 --> 47:29.846
Do you think dreams can just be had?

47:29.930 --> 47:33.016
Only those who have the luxury
to search for them can dream.

47:33.100 --> 47:37.020
Those who get the chance to rise again
after failure can pursue their dreams.

47:37.729 --> 47:41.024
You wouldn't know. You've always lived
in a Mediterranean climate.

47:41.483 --> 47:44.736
A clear, mild, and perfect environment.

47:45.320 --> 47:49.241
Me? Warmth is only momentary.
I'm stuck in Siberia most of the time..

47:50.325 --> 47:53.203
The winds are biting cold.
It snows, rains, and hails.

47:53.287 --> 47:55.372
- Do you know what that's like?
- I do know.

47:56.873 --> 47:58.709
I've had winters like that too.

47:58.792 --> 47:59.918
[leaves rustling]

48:04.965 --> 48:07.009
I thought you'd remember.

48:12.389 --> 48:14.141
[mellow music playing]

48:47.257 --> 48:48.342
You scared me.

48:49.468 --> 48:51.762
- Why are you here?
- I was waiting for you.

48:51.845 --> 48:53.764
Are you in puberty?
What's with your voice?

48:53.889 --> 48:56.892
It's your first day on the national team.
I'll let it slide.

48:58.769 --> 49:01.605
What are you doing?
Did you do something weird again?

49:01.688 --> 49:03.023
It's a gift.

49:08.195 --> 49:09.321
This towel's a gift?

49:09.404 --> 49:10.572
Yeah, open it up.

49:12.866 --> 49:15.494
CHOI SEUNG-HYO, 2008 BEIJING OLYMPICS
GO FOR GOLD

49:17.621 --> 49:18.497
Are you joking?

49:18.580 --> 49:19.414
Isn't it cool?

49:19.498 --> 49:21.458
I asked them to embroider it like that.

49:21.583 --> 49:23.919
- Take it to the training center.
- No way.

49:24.002 --> 49:25.087
What if someone sees?

49:28.173 --> 49:30.592
Fine, I'll take it. Okay?

49:31.510 --> 49:34.638
Take care of yourself.
Bring honor to your country.

49:34.721 --> 49:37.766
It's not like I'm going
to the Olympics tomorrow.

49:37.849 --> 49:39.685
Good luck! You got this!

49:41.186 --> 49:42.270
Good luck!

49:44.815 --> 49:46.608
You can do it!

49:46.692 --> 49:48.568
WE'LL REPAY YOUR SUPPORT WITH MEDALS

49:54.908 --> 49:55.909
[chuckles softly]

50:05.335 --> 50:06.420
[car accelerating]

50:07.295 --> 50:08.588
[horn honking]

50:08.672 --> 50:09.840
[tires screeching]

50:09.923 --> 50:11.133
- [thud]
- [glass breaking]

50:17.431 --> 50:18.265
[thuds]

50:18.974 --> 50:20.267
[gasping]

50:30.402 --> 50:31.445
[continues gasping]

50:34.072 --> 50:36.533
[male anchor] We bring you
some unfortunate news.

50:36.658 --> 50:40.704
Choi Seung-hyo, who secured his ticket
to the Olympics after winning

50:40.787 --> 50:42.873
the 2007 National Swimming Championships,

50:42.956 --> 50:45.083
has been involved in an accident.

50:45.167 --> 50:46.710
- Seung-hyo's okay.
- Seung-hyo…

50:49.045 --> 50:50.464
Seung-hyo… [whimpering]

50:50.547 --> 50:52.549
- [Mi-suk] It's okay.
- [Seok-ryu sobbing]

50:53.759 --> 50:55.761
[Mi-suk] It's okay. It'll be okay.

50:59.431 --> 51:00.557
It's okay, all right?

51:04.227 --> 51:07.814
[Gyeong-jong] With rehabilitation,
you'll be able to walk again.

51:08.982 --> 51:11.276
But I don't think
you'll be able to continue…

51:15.113 --> 51:16.490
your career as an athlete.

51:18.074 --> 51:19.743
[pop song playing]

51:25.665 --> 51:26.500
[door opens]

51:27.834 --> 51:28.668
[door closes]

51:34.883 --> 51:35.717
[exhales]

51:43.850 --> 51:44.768
[whimpering]

52:13.171 --> 52:14.130
[Seung-hyo] I do know.

52:15.799 --> 52:17.759
I've had winters like that too.

52:19.302 --> 52:21.263
I thought you'd remember.

52:21.346 --> 52:22.180
[exhales]

52:25.517 --> 52:26.810
[sighs]

52:46.329 --> 52:47.414
[inhales]

53:02.512 --> 53:03.430
[birds chirping]

53:14.190 --> 53:15.901
I left my phone in my office.

53:19.446 --> 53:22.490
- [door slides open, closes]
- [sighs softly]

53:27.621 --> 53:29.039
[Na-yun] I heard you two fought.

53:29.915 --> 53:31.583
Mr. Yoon told me.

53:32.834 --> 53:36.129
Why would he tell you about that?

53:36.212 --> 53:38.423
I have some talent in counseling.

53:39.799 --> 53:41.718
I've heard both sides.

53:41.801 --> 53:43.762
I think you're right.

53:44.429 --> 53:47.641
Covert plagiarism? That's so insulting!

53:47.724 --> 53:49.601
Moreover, a person should look ahead.

53:50.310 --> 53:52.479
We're going to succeed in the future.

53:52.562 --> 53:54.856
We can't have plagiarism issues
bring us down.

53:54.940 --> 53:57.776
- Are you taking my side?
- You should let me finish.

53:58.944 --> 54:00.528
However, Mr. Yoon's right too.

54:01.529 --> 54:05.200
I want to work nine-to-five
and get paid well.

54:05.283 --> 54:07.619
To do that, the company must do well.

54:07.702 --> 54:09.162
We have to hire more people too.

54:10.747 --> 54:13.959
Due to the nature of architecture,
we're always beholden to the client.

54:14.668 --> 54:17.671
But you don't know how to do that.

54:18.296 --> 54:19.714
Maybe you're too content.

54:22.550 --> 54:24.594
I heard something similar yesterday.

54:24.678 --> 54:26.388
Whoever they are, they were right.

54:26.471 --> 54:28.556
- You know it's true.
- What?

54:29.099 --> 54:30.016
Seung-hyo,

54:30.100 --> 54:31.101
you're marvelous.

54:32.143 --> 54:33.979
You speak beautifully like poetry.

54:34.062 --> 54:36.523
You're an idealist
who loves dreams more than reality.

54:37.774 --> 54:40.443
You're always so full of pride.

54:41.528 --> 54:43.863
But do you know
where all of that comes from?

54:45.824 --> 54:46.992
It comes from privilege.

54:48.535 --> 54:49.494
[Seok-ryu] Hey! Dreams?

54:50.078 --> 54:52.414
Do you think dreams can just be had?

54:52.497 --> 54:55.333
Only those who have the luxury
to search for them can dream.

54:55.417 --> 54:59.713
Those who get the chance to rise again
after failure can pursue their dreams.

54:59.796 --> 55:01.006
[pleasant music playing]

55:01.089 --> 55:02.799
[Na-yun] So in conclusion,

55:02.882 --> 55:05.969
for the development
and glory of Atelier In,

55:06.052 --> 55:08.972
I hope you two CEOs
can work together beautifully.

55:09.889 --> 55:11.433
Just so you know,

55:11.516 --> 55:13.935
Mr. Yoon stood outside
your door for a long time.

55:18.773 --> 55:20.775
- You're a great counselor.
- [Na-yun] I know.

55:26.114 --> 55:26.948
[sighs]

55:30.035 --> 55:30.869
[groaning]

55:32.704 --> 55:33.580
[knock on door]

55:34.831 --> 55:35.665
Come in.

55:41.337 --> 55:44.716
It looked like you didn't take your coffee
because of me earlier.

55:45.550 --> 55:49.220
Yeah, thanks.

55:50.513 --> 55:52.891
I'm sorry… [clears throat]
…about yesterday.

55:53.683 --> 55:55.143
I put you in a tough spot.

55:55.226 --> 55:57.395
No, it's fine.

55:57.479 --> 56:02.358
I know it was a bad call,
but I pretended otherwise.

56:04.319 --> 56:05.236
I'm so ashamed.

56:05.320 --> 56:09.449
Stop it. What are you saying?

56:10.408 --> 56:13.411
I was being selfish for personal reasons.
You were right.

56:14.746 --> 56:16.498
I wanted to work on the pool more.

56:18.666 --> 56:21.836
I thought it was my chance
to turn the page there

56:23.379 --> 56:26.716
I get it, and I gave it some thought.

56:28.176 --> 56:31.387
I thought about how you must've felt
when you quit swimming.

56:32.597 --> 56:34.599
I can't even imagine.

56:35.725 --> 56:36.643
[chuckles softly]

56:39.104 --> 56:41.564
Na-yun just told me…

56:43.233 --> 56:44.984
we'd both fail
if we ran separate companies.

56:45.568 --> 56:46.402
What?

56:47.028 --> 56:49.739
Unless we want to starve,
she said we should stick together.

56:49.823 --> 56:51.991
[laughs]

56:52.075 --> 56:55.370
She really does say whatever she wants.

56:55.453 --> 56:57.372
Millennials and Gen Z sure are different.

56:57.455 --> 56:58.748
- [Myeong-u laughing]
- [chuckles]

56:59.707 --> 57:02.085
Look, you're great and all,

57:02.669 --> 57:05.296
but don't talk about
millennials and Gen Z like that.

57:05.380 --> 57:06.381
[Myeong-u] What?

57:07.590 --> 57:09.467
Only old people do that.

57:09.551 --> 57:10.844
The kids don't care.

57:10.927 --> 57:14.180
So don't group them
as a generation like that.

57:14.264 --> 57:15.723
So you don't like me?

57:16.891 --> 57:18.184
You won't work with me?

57:18.268 --> 57:19.894
I'll do it. Why wouldn't I?

57:19.978 --> 57:22.814
[laughs] Yeah, I knew you would.

57:22.897 --> 57:24.482
You're too close.

57:24.566 --> 57:26.151
- I can't work like this.
- Okay.

57:27.068 --> 57:28.236
[chuckles]

57:28.319 --> 57:31.531
- I'm really sorry about yesterday.
- No, I'm sorry.

57:31.614 --> 57:33.283
[both laughing]

57:33.825 --> 57:35.702
- [leaves rustling]
- [indistinct chatter]

57:37.328 --> 57:38.329
[girl laughing]

57:39.789 --> 57:41.916
[pleasant music playing]

57:43.168 --> 57:44.002
There you go!

57:44.878 --> 57:47.422
[boys exclaiming, cheering]

57:52.385 --> 57:53.553
[indistinct chatter]

58:03.271 --> 58:04.939
[girl] Then, what was your dream?

58:06.024 --> 58:06.900
My dream?

58:07.525 --> 58:11.446
[girl] Yes. When you were in high school,
what did you want to be?

58:12.906 --> 58:16.743
Now that I have to answer,
I don't really know.

58:18.286 --> 58:22.290
Back then, just coming in first
in everything was my dream.

58:23.208 --> 58:25.710
I wanted to be a daughter
my mom could be proud of.

58:25.793 --> 58:28.087
I wanted my teachers to praise me.

58:28.880 --> 58:30.798
I wanted everyone to recognize me.

58:31.966 --> 58:35.720
Looking back now,
I feel a bit sorry for myself.

58:36.513 --> 58:37.514
Why?

58:37.597 --> 58:40.016
I cared about how others saw me,

58:40.099 --> 58:43.895
and I don't think I paid attention
to myself.

58:43.978 --> 58:45.146
[phone vibrating]

58:51.152 --> 58:54.072
THE RECRUITING TEAMS AT GLO KOREA
AND SERENDIPITY BOTH WANT INTERVIEWS

58:58.910 --> 59:00.912
[sighs deeply]

59:21.933 --> 59:23.184
[groaning]

59:24.936 --> 59:25.770
[exhales]

59:33.319 --> 59:34.529
[knife slicing]

59:35.780 --> 59:38.866
[Jae-suk] Is our family's knucklehead hero
finally up?

59:41.244 --> 59:42.328
I'm hungry.

59:42.412 --> 59:44.038
Are you hungry? [gasps]

59:44.122 --> 59:47.292
I just started the rice cooker.
It'll take some time.

59:47.375 --> 59:49.836
Eat some rice cakes on the table.

59:49.919 --> 59:50.753
[Mo-eum] What?

59:54.173 --> 59:56.801
[yawning] I've been eating rice cakes
so often lately.

59:57.385 --> 59:58.636
Who are they from?

59:58.720 --> 01:00:01.097
[Jae-suk] The new neighbor
who just moved in.

01:00:01.889 --> 01:00:05.018
Hey, I was the broker for that house.

01:00:05.602 --> 01:00:07.687
It was on the market for ages
with no prospects.

01:00:07.770 --> 01:00:10.148
I was so worried. Isn't it great?

01:00:10.231 --> 01:00:11.065
[Mo-eum] Mmm.

01:00:12.233 --> 01:00:13.318
[Jae-suk] Is it good?

01:00:13.401 --> 01:00:14.527
It's good.

01:00:14.611 --> 01:00:15.820
[pleasant music playing]

01:00:20.700 --> 01:00:21.659
[exhales]

01:00:38.885 --> 01:00:40.303
[mysterious music playing]

01:00:52.857 --> 01:00:54.525
[both screaming]

01:00:59.113 --> 01:01:01.157
Is that you, Seok-ryu?

01:01:02.200 --> 01:01:03.534
Ms. Yu?

01:01:05.662 --> 01:01:08.331
[Jin-ae] It's a pear and bellflower tea.
It's good for your throat.

01:01:08.414 --> 01:01:09.749
Thank you.

01:01:10.541 --> 01:01:12.418
I'm sorry about earlier. Did I scare you?

01:01:13.503 --> 01:01:18.841
It's okay. I'll stay cool for summer
with the chill you sent down my spine.

01:01:18.925 --> 01:01:20.301
[both chuckle]

01:01:20.385 --> 01:01:23.137
Speaking of which,
what were you looking for?

01:01:23.221 --> 01:01:25.556
[sighs] A time capsule.

01:01:25.640 --> 01:01:27.767
I buried it with Seung-hyo and Mo-eum.

01:01:27.850 --> 01:01:30.019
You all did something that cute?

01:01:30.895 --> 01:01:32.480
But you couldn't find it.

01:01:32.563 --> 01:01:34.315
It's for the best.

01:01:35.692 --> 01:01:37.860
I thought I'd find the answers
if I saw it.

01:01:38.903 --> 01:01:40.446
I think it'll just confuse me more.

01:01:41.114 --> 01:01:42.323
What?

01:01:42.407 --> 01:01:43.408
Ms. Yu,

01:01:44.409 --> 01:01:45.743
I lied to you.

01:01:47.662 --> 01:01:49.247
I don't work at Greip anymore.

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:52.250
I quit.

01:01:53.543 --> 01:02:00.174
To be honest, I don't know if I quit
or got chased out.

01:02:02.468 --> 01:02:03.302
[Jin-ae exhales]

01:02:04.721 --> 01:02:08.141
Seok-ryu, you've always done well.

01:02:08.224 --> 01:02:09.851
That's why I worried about you.

01:02:11.060 --> 01:02:14.397
What if you couldn't do something well?

01:02:14.480 --> 01:02:16.023
What would you do then?

01:02:16.107 --> 01:02:17.316
[mellow music playing]

01:02:17.400 --> 01:02:19.986
I don't think I taught you how to do that.

01:02:20.903 --> 01:02:23.865
But I realized something
after being a teacher for so long.

01:02:24.574 --> 01:02:26.617
Children keep growing.

01:02:27.702 --> 01:02:29.537
Even if I don't teach them,

01:02:29.620 --> 01:02:32.832
they all find the answers
on their own somehow.

01:02:36.335 --> 01:02:39.172
Was there an answer you thought about
when you quit?

01:02:40.256 --> 01:02:43.217
Then, don't change your mind.
Trust your choice and move on.

01:02:44.594 --> 01:02:46.053
Changing it always ends up wrong.

01:02:46.137 --> 01:02:47.054
[both chuckle]

01:02:47.138 --> 01:02:47.972
You're right.

01:02:49.682 --> 01:02:51.976
Go to the pool when you're done.

01:02:52.059 --> 01:02:53.186
I think Seung-hyo's there.

01:02:54.479 --> 01:02:55.313
Okay.

01:03:04.238 --> 01:03:05.323
Hey, Seung-hyo!

01:03:06.115 --> 01:03:07.867
Did you find the time capsule?

01:03:07.950 --> 01:03:10.077
You scared me. What are you doing here?

01:03:10.161 --> 01:03:11.621
I should be asking you that.

01:03:12.413 --> 01:03:16.501
Hey, what's that in your hand?
Is that my letter?

01:03:22.840 --> 01:03:24.592
"To Bae Seok-ryu ten years from now."

01:03:24.675 --> 01:03:25.593
"Hi!"

01:03:25.676 --> 01:03:27.512
- "I'm the best and most beautiful…
- Hey!

01:03:27.595 --> 01:03:29.388
- "Bae Seok-ryu!"
- Don't read that. Hey!

01:03:29.472 --> 01:03:31.474
- "What am I like in the future?"
- I'll kill you!

01:03:31.557 --> 01:03:34.602
"I'm imprisoned in a classroom
due to the crime of being a student."

01:03:34.685 --> 01:03:36.395
- Hey, don't run! You'll slip!
- No!

01:03:36.479 --> 01:03:39.232
- Don't read my letter!
- "My school uniform's a prison uniform."

01:03:39.315 --> 01:03:41.567
I was crazy. What did I write? Hey!

01:03:41.651 --> 01:03:43.569
[Seung-hyo] "I'm punished
with school work."

01:03:43.653 --> 01:03:45.988
- "I'll be released with graduation."
- [Seok-ryu] Give it!

01:03:46.072 --> 01:03:47.824
"The best and the first."

01:03:47.907 --> 01:03:49.867
- "Do you know they're similar?"
- Are you kidding?

01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:51.619
- "If you've done your best,
- Hey!

01:03:51.702 --> 01:03:53.162
"And you'll probably come in first."

01:03:53.246 --> 01:03:54.580
I told you to stop!

01:03:54.664 --> 01:03:56.499
We should've kept this buried.

01:03:56.582 --> 01:03:59.043
They'll put this in textbooks
if they find this later.

01:03:59.126 --> 01:04:02.463
A statement that will go down in history.
It's truly a gem!

01:04:02.547 --> 01:04:04.507
Gem, my foot! Give it to me.

01:04:05.508 --> 01:04:06.342
Give it to me!

01:04:06.926 --> 01:04:07.760
Are you crazy?

01:04:10.429 --> 01:04:12.098
Wow, that's low.

01:04:13.307 --> 01:04:15.768
Did you jump knowing I can't swim?

01:04:15.852 --> 01:04:17.478
Come in and take it from me then.

01:04:17.562 --> 01:04:19.522
No, I'm scared of the water.

01:04:21.315 --> 01:04:22.149
Did you know?

01:04:23.192 --> 01:04:24.485
After I quit swimming,

01:04:25.403 --> 01:04:27.029
this is my first time in a pool.

01:04:29.407 --> 01:04:31.784
Wow, why didn't I come in until now?

01:04:31.868 --> 01:04:33.077
It's so nice.

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:37.874
Hey, I didn't mean what I said before--

01:04:37.957 --> 01:04:38.833
Do you remember?

01:04:40.126 --> 01:04:41.586
When I couldn't swim anymore

01:04:43.170 --> 01:04:44.922
and I was cooped up in my room?

01:04:45.006 --> 01:04:46.549
[mellow music playing]

01:04:46.632 --> 01:04:48.134
[Seok-ryu] Hey, what are you doing?

01:04:49.594 --> 01:04:52.346
I brought some comics.
Let's read them together.

01:04:53.055 --> 01:04:54.974
Then, I'll make you some ramyun instead.

01:04:55.725 --> 01:04:57.059
No eggs, just how you like it.

01:04:59.562 --> 01:05:01.606
What are you doing? Hey!

01:05:01.689 --> 01:05:03.858
Why are you pushing me?
I have to read that.

01:05:03.941 --> 01:05:08.154
- Seung-hyo, at least give me my comics.
- [locks door]

01:05:10.698 --> 01:05:11.866
[footsteps approaching]

01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:14.577
[closet opens]

01:05:15.536 --> 01:05:17.204
[key rattling]

01:05:17.997 --> 01:05:18.915
[Seung-hyo groans]

01:05:19.624 --> 01:05:22.585
Did you think I couldn't come in
if you locked your door?

01:05:22.668 --> 01:05:25.671
I knew the keys were
in the top shelf of the shoe cabinet!

01:05:29.091 --> 01:05:31.427
Okay, instead of ramyun,
I'll buy you barbecue!

01:05:31.510 --> 01:05:33.512
I'll buy you meat! How does that sound?

01:05:34.889 --> 01:05:35.806
[groans softly]

01:05:36.849 --> 01:05:39.727
Hey! Wait! Hey!

01:05:41.395 --> 01:05:42.313
[locks door]

01:05:42.396 --> 01:05:46.901
Hey! Do you think I'll give up like this?

01:05:47.526 --> 01:05:48.778
[objects clattering]

01:06:06.754 --> 01:06:07.588
What are you doing?

01:06:08.172 --> 01:06:09.715
[yelling] My gosh!

01:06:10.716 --> 01:06:12.802
- Seriously?
- [Seok-ryu] You really scared me.

01:06:12.885 --> 01:06:14.345
[Seung-hyo] What are you doing?

01:06:14.428 --> 01:06:15.513
[Seok-ryu] Move over.

01:06:15.596 --> 01:06:17.807
- [Seung-hyo] Come on!
- [Seok-ryu] Move out of the way.

01:06:17.890 --> 01:06:19.141
[both grunting]

01:06:20.768 --> 01:06:22.228
- [Seok-ryu sighs]
- [Seung-hyo groans]

01:06:22.812 --> 01:06:23.813
[Seok-ryu laughing]

01:06:28.859 --> 01:06:29.902
You're insane.

01:06:31.195 --> 01:06:33.656
Are you really laughing right now?

01:06:33.739 --> 01:06:35.700
Why would you climb up here like that?

01:06:35.783 --> 01:06:37.243
- You almost died!
- [laughing]

01:06:37.827 --> 01:06:40.454
Yeah, so why would you lock
your doors, you jerk?

01:06:40.538 --> 01:06:41.872
I almost died because of you.

01:06:41.956 --> 01:06:44.250
I just saved your life.
You're so ungrateful.

01:06:44.333 --> 01:06:46.293
You're such a lunatic.

01:06:46.377 --> 01:06:48.546
If I'm a lunatic, what are you? A bear?

01:06:48.629 --> 01:06:51.549
Did you think you'd turn into a human
after 100 years in your cave?

01:06:51.632 --> 01:06:54.885
You fossilized trilobite-looking fool.
You've regressed into a baby.

01:06:55.469 --> 01:06:56.804
A baby?

01:06:56.887 --> 01:06:58.973
You're the one who's like a Neanderthal.

01:06:59.056 --> 01:07:01.267
Do you lack the brain capacity?

01:07:01.350 --> 01:07:04.645
You can't distinguish between
what you can and can't do, can you?

01:07:04.729 --> 01:07:05.646
[quirky music playing]

01:07:05.730 --> 01:07:08.607
[sniffs] What is this smell?

01:07:08.691 --> 01:07:11.277
Is it mugwort and garlic? No.

01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:12.737
It smells like a lonely old man!

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:14.030
I don't smell anything.

01:07:14.113 --> 01:07:16.365
Shut up and get lost.
Go back to where you came.

01:07:16.449 --> 01:07:20.244
If I get lost, are you going to stare
at the wall like a loser again?

01:07:22.496 --> 01:07:24.623
- Loser?
- Yeah, you stupid dumbass loser.

01:07:24.707 --> 01:07:26.250
- Stop it.
- No.

01:07:26.333 --> 01:07:28.461
Dummy. You're the biggest loser
in the world, bitch.

01:07:28.544 --> 01:07:30.463
- Don't cuss.
- What are you going to do about it?

01:07:30.546 --> 01:07:33.507
Go and eat from your dog bowl,
you bastard.

01:07:33.591 --> 01:07:35.968
What's wrong with you?
I told you not to cuss!

01:07:36.052 --> 01:07:38.971
You damn loser. You're so dim-witted.

01:07:39.680 --> 01:07:40.973
I told you not to cuss.

01:07:41.057 --> 01:07:43.434
- What are you, five years old?
- [Seung-hyo groans]

01:07:43.517 --> 01:07:44.393
You stupid… [bleep]

01:07:44.477 --> 01:07:46.520
Damn it, I said stop!

01:07:46.604 --> 01:07:48.022
You think you're cool, don't you?

01:07:48.105 --> 01:07:50.107
You're frustrating and meek, you bastard.

01:07:50.191 --> 01:07:52.234
Damn it, I already feel like crap.

01:07:52.318 --> 01:07:55.863
- Why are you here bitching at me?
- You're the one acting like a damn fool.

01:07:55.946 --> 01:07:58.074
Damn it, I'm hurt and can't do anything.

01:07:58.157 --> 01:08:01.535
Why are you here bitching at me?
Do you even know how I feel?

01:08:01.619 --> 01:08:04.580
Do you even know what I'm going through?

01:08:05.623 --> 01:08:06.457
[sighs]

01:08:07.124 --> 01:08:08.292
Do you feel better now?

01:08:13.464 --> 01:08:16.383
[sighs] It's my first time
hearing your voice in a month.

01:08:18.260 --> 01:08:19.720
So what?

01:08:24.225 --> 01:08:26.769
Hey. Why do you have that in your bag?

01:08:26.852 --> 01:08:28.354
Lock your door again,

01:08:29.605 --> 01:08:30.773
and I'll break it down.

01:08:42.284 --> 01:08:43.536
[grunts] Damn it.

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:46.664
[exhales]

01:08:49.500 --> 01:08:50.709
[pleasant music playing]

01:08:52.503 --> 01:08:53.420
[chuckles softly]

01:08:54.380 --> 01:08:55.631
That's who you were.

01:08:56.715 --> 01:09:01.137
A damn lunatic wielding an ax
at a bear who trapped himself in a cave.

01:09:03.389 --> 01:09:04.682
That's your identity.

01:09:04.765 --> 01:09:06.517
Stop cowering. It doesn't suit you.

01:09:07.601 --> 01:09:09.979
- You call that words of comfort?
- It means you stink.

01:09:10.062 --> 01:09:10.938
What?

01:09:11.021 --> 01:09:13.524
The old Seok-ryu was lively and energetic.

01:09:14.275 --> 01:09:16.735
But you're so bland now.

01:09:16.819 --> 01:09:19.071
- [scoffs]
- You're no fun. You're boring.

01:09:19.155 --> 01:09:21.866
You'd better take that back.

01:09:26.078 --> 01:09:26.954
[footsteps]

01:09:31.625 --> 01:09:33.794
- [exhales]
- [exhilarating music playing]

01:09:42.720 --> 01:09:44.138
[yelps] Hey!

01:09:45.514 --> 01:09:47.474
- Hey…
- [Seok-ryu groaning]

01:09:48.809 --> 01:09:49.643
[Seung-hyo] Hey…

01:09:50.853 --> 01:09:51.687
Wait! Hey!

01:09:55.232 --> 01:09:56.692
[Seok-ryu] Help me!

01:09:57.526 --> 01:09:58.611
[screaming]

01:09:59.195 --> 01:10:00.112
Help me!

01:10:00.196 --> 01:10:03.240
- [screaming]
- I got you! You won't die. It's okay.

01:10:04.825 --> 01:10:05.910
[grunts]

01:10:05.993 --> 01:10:06.827
Damn it!

01:10:07.870 --> 01:10:11.248
Why would you jump in if you can't swim?

01:10:11.332 --> 01:10:13.792
Why would you piss me off like that?

01:10:13.876 --> 01:10:15.836
- Do you know why you're sinking?
- No!

01:10:15.920 --> 01:10:20.382
It's because your body's tense!
Relax a little! Relax!

01:10:20.466 --> 01:10:23.928
I can't relax when I get a shot
at the doctor's! How do I do it now?

01:10:24.011 --> 01:10:26.680
Wait, just… Yeah.
Pretend you're a jellyfish.

01:10:26.764 --> 01:10:29.141
Sway your limbs.
Yeah, just let the water take you.

01:10:30.309 --> 01:10:32.019
- Sway? Like this?
- Yeah.

01:10:32.102 --> 01:10:33.854
There you go. Like that.

01:10:33.938 --> 01:10:37.733
What? I think pretending
to be a jellyfish is working.

01:10:37.816 --> 01:10:39.818
- It's working. Yeah.
- It's working.

01:10:39.902 --> 01:10:43.155
It's not working! It's not! [screaming]
It's not working!

01:10:44.490 --> 01:10:45.324
My head!

01:10:46.033 --> 01:10:47.785
Hey! I drank some water!

01:10:47.868 --> 01:10:49.203
[Seung-hyo coughs]

01:10:49.286 --> 01:10:51.205
Don't grab my hair. Please.

01:10:57.795 --> 01:10:59.797
Am I really floating right now?

01:11:00.881 --> 01:11:03.801
This is so cool! Wow. I feel so strange.

01:11:05.219 --> 01:11:07.763
Do you want to keep talking
even in this moment?

01:11:08.347 --> 01:11:09.974
Feel the stillness in the water.

01:11:11.267 --> 01:11:12.476
[pleasant music playing]

01:11:15.312 --> 01:11:16.313
Hey, Seung-hyo?

01:11:17.106 --> 01:11:18.107
[Seung-hyo] What?

01:11:18.899 --> 01:11:20.818
I was actually nervous.

01:11:22.278 --> 01:11:24.363
I wanted to quit because I was exhausted.

01:11:25.072 --> 01:11:27.491
I wanted to rest and dream of a new life.

01:11:28.367 --> 01:11:29.410
But…

01:11:30.536 --> 01:11:35.124
I felt like nothing
without my Greip background.

01:11:37.710 --> 01:11:39.712
Everyone is moving forward,

01:11:41.380 --> 01:11:43.048
but I'm the only one who's stopped.

01:11:44.508 --> 01:11:46.593
That's how I felt after I quit swimming.

01:11:47.803 --> 01:11:50.431
The start signal had sounded,

01:11:51.015 --> 01:11:54.601
but I felt like I was standing alone
at the starting line.

01:11:55.769 --> 01:11:56.854
I thought,

01:11:58.856 --> 01:12:03.986
"It's going to be hard to find a place
where I can swim freely again."

01:12:05.571 --> 01:12:06.739
But you found it.

01:12:06.822 --> 01:12:07.823
I know.

01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:10.743
I found it, so why can't you?

01:12:11.660 --> 01:12:15.789
I hated going into bathwater,
but I'm able to jump back in again.

01:12:17.541 --> 01:12:18.500
You think so?

01:12:19.710 --> 01:12:21.879
Can I swim somewhere new too?

01:12:23.088 --> 01:12:23.922
Of course.

01:12:24.965 --> 01:12:27.634
Hey, I'm just curious.

01:12:30.304 --> 01:12:31.347
Hypothetically.

01:12:32.431 --> 01:12:36.018
Let's say you could swim again.

01:12:37.644 --> 01:12:38.937
If that were to happen,

01:12:40.647 --> 01:12:42.274
would you still be an architect?

01:12:44.693 --> 01:12:45.903
Yeah.

01:12:45.986 --> 01:12:47.905
- Really?
- Of course.

01:12:49.239 --> 01:12:50.532
What about you?

01:12:50.616 --> 01:12:52.242
- What?
- Hypothetically.

01:12:52.826 --> 01:12:54.912
Let's say you go back to before you quit.

01:12:56.288 --> 01:12:58.332
If you can go back to Greip,

01:12:59.375 --> 01:13:00.250
will you go back?

01:13:02.294 --> 01:13:03.545
No.

01:13:03.629 --> 01:13:04.630
One more.

01:13:06.548 --> 01:13:07.591
Hypothetically.

01:13:09.343 --> 01:13:11.678
Let's say you go back to before
your engagement was broken,

01:13:13.764 --> 01:13:14.681
what would you do?

01:13:17.518 --> 01:13:20.479
No. I wouldn't go back.

01:13:20.562 --> 01:13:21.438
[yelps]

01:13:26.860 --> 01:13:27.694
Okay, then.

01:13:32.032 --> 01:13:33.409
[pleasant music playing]

01:13:33.492 --> 01:13:36.787
We'll write letters to our future selves
ten years from now.

01:13:36.870 --> 01:13:37.913
[Mo-eum] Okay.

01:13:38.497 --> 01:13:39.581
Do we have to?

01:13:39.665 --> 01:13:40.958
Shut up and write.

01:13:41.542 --> 01:13:44.336
Let's open it in ten years.

01:13:44.420 --> 01:13:48.507
If anyone opens it before then,
they'll have bad luck for 1,000 years!

01:13:48.590 --> 01:13:50.259
Pinky swear! No take backs!

01:14:02.896 --> 01:14:04.898
Hi, Bae Seok-ryu ten years from now.

01:14:04.982 --> 01:14:07.734
It's me. The best and most beautiful.
Bae Seok-ryu!

01:14:08.694 --> 01:14:11.905
[Mo-eum] What if I can shoot webs
with the advancement of technology?

01:14:12.906 --> 01:14:15.367
There's a rumor you climb on the ceilings.

01:14:46.732 --> 01:14:49.318
[Seung-hyo] Ten years from now
feels so far away.

01:14:50.861 --> 01:14:53.947
By then, you probably told Seok-ryu
how you felt, right?

01:14:55.199 --> 01:14:56.575
[music continues playing]

01:15:08.086 --> 01:15:12.090
STOP LINE

01:15:12.174 --> 01:15:17.179
STARTING LINE

01:15:17.262 --> 01:15:18.555
[pop song playing]

01:15:47.960 --> 01:15:52.172
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:15:52.256 --> 01:15:54.758
[Seung-hyo] But still, how could I
leave evidence like that?

01:15:54.841 --> 01:15:56.843
Those feelings have long since expired.

01:15:56.927 --> 01:15:58.804
You finally opened it after all this time?

01:15:58.887 --> 01:16:01.056
I dug it up that night. I was curious.

01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:04.351
Greip contacted us!

01:16:05.394 --> 01:16:07.521
I moved here recently.
It's so nice to run in to you.

01:16:07.604 --> 01:16:08.605
Really?

01:16:08.689 --> 01:16:10.524
It's the reporter again.

01:16:10.607 --> 01:16:12.276
Have our tastes overlapped again?

01:16:12.943 --> 01:16:14.695
[Seok-ryu] No matter how hard you try,

01:16:14.778 --> 01:16:15.988
it's a waste of time.

01:16:16.071 --> 01:16:18.490
Don't talk about my hard work like that.

01:16:18.574 --> 01:16:19.575
Seok-ryu?

01:16:21.451 --> 01:16:22.578
Seung-hyo!

01:16:22.661 --> 01:16:24.121
What the hell did you just say?

01:16:27.457 --> 01:16:30.460
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
